<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Derge Gonchen Monastery</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">15th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Lhundrup Teng</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Derge Gonchen Monastery, also called Lhundrup Teng, is a Sakya monastery in Dêgê in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kham">Kham</a>, eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>, founded in the 15th century. The royal family of Derge rose around it and made it their seat, and it stands beside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derge-parkhang">Derge Parkhang</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> house founded by the kings in 1729. It remains the principal monastery of the town.</p></div>
